<p>NOTE: The company said improved operating results compared to 1996 are attributable to the benefits of legislation enacted in 1996. While the legislation has been in effect for the entire first six months of 1997, the pari-mutuel tax reduction did not become effective until after the second quarter of last year on July l, 1996. Pari-mutuel tax expense was $9,250 and $20,986, for the three month and six month periods ended June 30, 1997, respectively. These expense amounts are $226,862 and $373,310 lower than pari-mutuel taxes for the comparable periods, respectively, in 1996. However, this portion of the legislation also benefits the Horsepersons' purse funds, which receive a higher percentage of pari-mutuel take-out.  This results in higher statutory purse expense for the company.</p>
